---
import MarketingLayout from '../../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Code Signing Policy — kindling Writer"
  description="kindling's code signing policy. macOS builds are signed with an Apple Developer ID and notarized; Windows builds are not yet signed while SignPath is set up."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <h1>Code Signing Policy</h1>
    <p class="page-hero-subtext">How kindling's installers are signed to verify authenticity and integrity.</p>
  </section>

  <article class="content-section policy-content">
    <h2>macOS</h2>
    <p>kindling's macOS installer is <strong>signed with an Apple Developer ID</strong> and <strong>notarized by Apple</strong>. This means macOS Gatekeeper will allow the app to open without any security workarounds. The universal DMG works on both Apple Silicon and Intel Macs.</p>
  </article>

  <section class="content-section alt policy-content">
    <h2>Windows</h2>
    <p>kindling's Windows builds are <strong>not yet code-signed</strong>. Signing through <a href="https://about.signpath.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SignPath.io</a>, with a certificate from <a href="https://signpath.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SignPath Foundation</a>, is being finalized. Until it is in place, Windows SmartScreen may show a warning for unrecognized apps. Click "More info" → "Run anyway" to proceed, as described in the <a href="/docs/installation/#bypassing-smartscreen">installation guide</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section policy-content">
    <h2>Team roles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Committer, reviewer, and approver:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/smith-and-web" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Josh Smith</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section alt policy-content">
    <h2>Build process</h2>
    <p>All signed artifacts are built using <a href="https://github.com/smith-and-web/kindling/blob/main/.github/workflows/release.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Actions</a> on GitHub-hosted runners. The build process is fully automated and reproducible. No locally built artifacts are signed.</p>
    <p>Source code: <a href="https://github.com/smith-and-web/kindling" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/smith-and-web/kindling</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section alt policy-content">
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>This program transfers information to other networked systems only to check for and download updates, and when the user chooses to submit feedback.</p>
    <p>kindling has no analytics or telemetry and does not upload manuscripts. All project files remain on the user's computer. See our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for what a feedback submission includes.</p>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .policy-content strong { color: var(--color-text); }
  .policy-content ul { margin: 16px 0; padding-left: 24px; }
  .policy-content li { margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: var(--leading); }
  .policy-content a { color: var(--color-accent-text); text-decoration: underline; }
  .policy-content a:hover { color: var(--color-text); }
</style>
